# Liriel Dawnsong's camp talks (story/camp_talk.gd): offered after a Long Rest once the opening `if` holds; each
# plays once. Quest: Carry the Dawn (narrative/companions/dawn.dialogue). The file offers its first talk that holds:
# when she's Strained or Doubtful (story/approval.gd), those first; then the quest's; then Warm, Close and Devoted.

# --- After Strahd called Liriel to kneel at the night visit (strahd/visits:night_kneel) -------------------------------

~ talk_knelt
if name:liriel_dawnsong and flag.strahd_knelt == "liriel_dawnsong"
-> knelt
endif
-> END

~ knelt
Narrator: Liriel is up before anyone, kneeling in the cold grass with her holy symbol in both hands. She isn't praying. She is staring at her own knees.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I knelt to him. I kneel every morning of my life, and last night my knees didn't know the difference.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: My faith has never once been asked to bend. He didn't ask. He just bent it, and handed it back.
* You didn't choose it, Liriel. -> knelt_choose
* Then we make sure he never gets that close again. -> knelt_close

~ knelt_choose
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: No. That's what frightens me. Faith was always the thing I chose. Every morning, I chose it.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: So I'll choose it again tomorrow. And the day after. He can't take a thing I keep picking up.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You told me I didn't choose to kneel to Strahd
-> END

~ knelt_close
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Wake me if he comes. Wake me first. I want to be standing when he looks at me again.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2: You promised he'd never get that close to me again
-> END

# --- When she's lost faith in the party (approval) ----------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_strained
if name:liriel_dawnsong and approval.liriel_dawnsong <= strained
-> strained
endif
-> END

~ strained
Narrator: Liriel doesn't kneel at the edge of the camp tonight. She sits in the middle of it, close to the fire, with her little light cupped in her hands, and looks at each of you in turn as if she were counting.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I've tried to find a kind way to say this, and there isn't one, so I'll say it as plainly as Thistle would.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I can't hear Him here. I told you that. And now I can't hear the dawn in any of you, either. I look at what we've done, and I can't find it.
if flag.dark_gifts_taken >= 1
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: We let a thing in the amber put its gift into one of us. It's still there. I feel it when I pray, like a draught under a door.
elif flag.abbot_fate == "wedding"
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: We stood and watched an angel give a dead girl to the devil. I keep seeing the dress.
endif
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I'll heal you. I'll stand with you. But I won't sing in his chapel with you behind me like this. It would be a lie, and He would know, and so would the dawn.
* Then show us the way back. -> strained_way
* We hear you. We'll mend it. -> strained_mend
* We don't need your hymn. -> strained_cold

~ strained_way
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Be kind on purpose. That's the whole of it. It isn't easy; it's only simple, which people mistake for easy.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Thank you for asking. Asking is the first step of every road I know.
approve liriel_dawnsong +10: You asked me to show you the way back
-> END

~ strained_mend
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Then let it be so. I'll watch, and I'll hope. I'm very good at both; I've had practice.
approve liriel_dawnsong +6: You told me you'd mend it
-> END

~ strained_cold
Narrator: She doesn't answer. She cups the little light closer, and turns her face away from all of you, toward the place where the east ought to be.
approve liriel_dawnsong -5: You told me you don't need my hymn
-> END

~ talk_doubt
if name:liriel_dawnsong and approval.liriel_dawnsong == doubtful
-> doubt
endif
-> END

~ doubt
Narrator: Liriel says the evening prayer in a whisper tonight, and when it's done she doesn't put her holy symbol away. She sits turning it in her fingers.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: May I ask you something? You needn't answer tonight.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: When we came into this valley I thought we were carrying the dawn together. Lately I'm not certain we're walking toward it.
if flag.bella_pact
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: We shook hands with a fiend at that mill. I said it aloud so none of us would forget. I haven't.
endif
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I'm not angry. I'm frightened, a little, and I'd rather be frightened out loud than in the dark. You know how I feel about the dark.
* You're right to ask. We've lost our way a little. -> doubt_lost
* The dawn won't come by being gentle, Liriel. -> doubt_gentle
* Your god isn't in charge of us. -> doubt_god

~ doubt_lost
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: A little is a good word. A little can be walked back. Thank you. Be at peace.
approve liriel_dawnsong +6: You admitted we'd lost our way a little
-> END

~ doubt_gentle
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Perhaps not. But it won't come by being cruel, either. I've looked. It isn't down that road.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1: You told me the dawn won't come by being gentle
-> END

~ doubt_god
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: No. He isn't in charge of anyone. That was never the point of Him. ...I thought you knew that.
approve liriel_dawnsong -4: You told me my god isn't in charge of you
-> END

# --- Her quest ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_silence
if name:liriel_dawnsong and quest.carry_the_dawn == the_vision
-> silence
endif
-> END

~ silence
Narrator: Liriel is awake before anyone, kneeling at the edge of the camp facing east, where the dawn would be if this valley had one. Her lips are moving. After a while they stop.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Morning's grace. I'm sorry. I didn't mean to wake anyone.
* Is something wrong? -> silence_wrong
* (Kneel beside her.) -> silence_kneel

~ silence_kneel
Narrator: You kneel beside her in the wet grass. She doesn't look round, but she moves over a little, to make room.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1: You knelt beside me in the wet grass
-> silence_wrong

~ silence_wrong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: He answers. That's the strange part. I pray for healing and the healing comes. I pray for light and the light comes. Everything works.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: But he isn't here. At home I'd pray and he'd be in the room, the way you can tell someone's in the next room with the door shut. Here the door is shut and there's no next room. There's just the door.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I've never prayed into a silence before. It's very loud.
* Maybe that's why you were sent. To be the next room. -> silence_sent
* He sent you here. He knew it would be like this. -> silence_knew
* Do you want to stop? -> silence_stop

~ silence_sent
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: ...Oh.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: That's either very wise or very silly, and I can't tell which, and I think that means it's wise. Thank you.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2: You told me I might be the next room
-> silence_end

~ silence_knew
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Yes. He always knows. That's the comfort of him. It's also, I'm learning, the difficulty.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1: You reminded me He knew what He was sending me into
-> silence_end

~ silence_stop
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Stop? No. Oh, no. You don't stop talking to someone you love because they've gone quiet. That's when you talk more.
approve liriel_dawnsong -1: You asked me whether I wanted to stop praying
-> silence_end

~ silence_end
if not (quest.carry_the_dawn >= the_silence)
quest carry_the_dawn the_silence
endif
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I'll pray with you tomorrow, if you like. I don't know any of the words. I'll hum.
interject name:thistle: Your god's like a deer, Sunbeam. You go quiet and still and wait, and they come out. Grandda says.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: For what it's worth, my... the people I'm in business with... they're very loud. All the time. I'd take quiet.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: The dawn comes. It always comes. I'll just have to be patient about where.
-> END

~ talk_dark
if name:liriel_dawnsong and quest.carry_the_dawn >= the_silence and flag.eva_truth_teller != "liriel_dawnsong"
-> dark
endif
-> END

~ dark
Narrator: The watch changes in the small hours, and there's a light burning in Liriel's bedroll: a tiny one, the size of a candle flame, cupped against her chest. Her eyes are open.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Oh. Don't mind me. It's a devotional light. The Morninglord likes a lamp lit.
* [Insight DC 10] It isn't, is it? -> dark_truth | dark_truth
* Goodnight, Liriel. -> dark_leave

~ dark_truth
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: ...No. It isn't. I'm frightened of the dark. I have been since I was very small. A priestess of the dawn, afraid of the dark. You'd think it would be funny. It is, a little.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: And now I've come to the darkest place in the world on purpose, and every night it's very, very dark.
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: I'll sleep next to you. I sleep light. Anything comes, I'll bite it.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: That's very kind, dear heart. Please don't bite anything near my face.
elif name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I'll sit up with you. I'm big. The dark has to get past me first. I've never lost a staring contest with the dark.
else
Narrator: Someone sits down beside her and stays until morning, and nobody mentions it the next day.
endif
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Being brave isn't not being afraid. I know that. I've told it to a hundred novices. It turns out it's much easier to say.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You saw through my devotional light, and sat with me anyway
-> END

~ dark_leave
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Goodnight. Be at peace.
-> END

~ talk_faith
if name:liriel_dawnsong and quest.carry_the_dawn >= the_fall and flag.abbot_fate
-> faith
endif
-> END

~ faith
Narrator: Liriel hasn't said much since the abbey. Tonight she sits with her holy symbol in her lap, not praying, just turning it so the firelight runs round the rim.
if flag.abbot_fate == "repentant"
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: He remembered. In the end, he remembered the sun. He laid her down and went up the mountain to wait for judgement, and I think he'll get mercy, and I think he knows it, and I think that frightens him more.
elif flag.abbot_fate == "wedding"
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: We let him do it. We stood there and let an angel of the Morninglord give a dead girl to the devil in white, and call it love. I keep seeing the dress.
elif flag.abbot_fate == "slain"
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: We killed an angel. I helped. I'd do it again. I don't know what that makes me, and I'm not going to pretend I don't mind.
else
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: He sits in his church and won't speak. An angel. In the dark, with nobody to pray to. I'd have thought that couldn't happen to one of them.
endif
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I always thought heaven was... finished. Perfect. That the messengers were the safe part. And here's one who stayed too long in the dark and forgot what he was for.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: If an angel can fall here, then nobody is coming to fix Barovia. Not him. Not anyone from above.
* Then it's up to us. -> faith_us
* Does that shake your faith? -> faith_shake

~ faith_shake
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: It shook it. I could feel it go, like a bell. And then it rang.
-> faith_us

~ faith_us
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Yes. That's what I've decided. He didn't send me here to watch an angel do it. He sent me because there wasn't one. The dawn doesn't come down from above. It gets carried.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: So I'll carry it. All the way up to the castle, if I have to, and I'll sing it in his chapel.
if not (quest.carry_the_dawn >= faith_kept)
quest carry_the_dawn faith_kept
endif
approve liriel_dawnsong +2: You told me the rest is up to us
interject name:wren_featherfoot: You're scarier than you look, you know that?
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Everyone says that. I've never understood why it surprises them.
-> END

# --- As she comes to trust the party (approval) -------------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_warm
if name:liriel_dawnsong and approval.liriel_dawnsong >= warm and level >= 3
-> warm
endif
-> END

~ warm
Narrator: Liriel is teaching the morning hymn to whoever will hold still. So far that is nobody, but she's undeterred.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: It's only four lines. The novices learn it at six years old. Some of them learn it at five and are insufferable about it.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: You sing it facing east, even when there's no east to speak of. Especially then. That's the point of it, I think. I didn't understand that until I came here.
* (Learn the hymn.) -> warm_learn
* Sing it for us. -> warm_sing
* There's no east in Barovia, Liriel. -> warm_east

~ warm_learn
Narrator: You get the first line wrong, and the second line very wrong, and she corrects you both times without a flicker of impatience. The third line comes out right. She looks as proud as if you'd raised the dead.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: There. Now there are two of us facing east. That's a congregation, technically.
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: I'll whistle it. Through my fingers. Sunbeam taught me. No, I taught her. We taught each other.
endif
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You learned the morning hymn with me
-> END

~ warm_sing
Narrator: She sings it softly, so as not to wake the others, and the fire seems to lean toward her to listen.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: It sounds better at dawn. Everything does. That's rather the point of dawn.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2: You asked me to sing the morning hymn
-> END

~ warm_east
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: There's always an east. It's only very shy here. You have to be patient with shy things.
approve liriel_dawnsong +1: You argued with me about the east, which nobody's done since I was six
-> END

~ talk_close
if name:liriel_dawnsong and approval.liriel_dawnsong >= close and level >= 5
-> close
endif
-> END

~ close
Narrator: It's very late. Liriel is awake, which isn't unusual. What's unusual is that she comes and sits beside you, and doesn't pretend she's praying.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I've never told anyone this. Not my abbess. Not the Morninglord, though He knows, of course. He knows everything. It's very inconvenient.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I'm afraid the vision was only a dream I wanted. A girl who'd sung the sun up every morning of her life, dreaming she was important enough to be sent somewhere.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: If it was only a dream, then I brought you all here for nothing. I brought myself here for nothing.
* Dream or not, you came. That's what matters. -> close_came
* We'd have come anyway. -> close_anyway
* We've seen what you've done here. That's no dream. -> close_seen

~ close_came
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: That's very nearly a sermon. I'll steal it for the novices, if I ever see them again. I'll say a wise friend told me.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You told me it matters that I came
-> close_end

~ close_anyway
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Would you? Into this? ...Yes. I think you would. That's either very brave or very foolish, and I find I don't mind which.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2: You told me you'd have come anyway
-> close_end

~ close_seen
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: The bones. The children in the house. The little lights. ...Yes. Those weren't dreams. I was there for those. So were you.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You reminded me what we've done here isn't a dream
-> close_end

~ close_end
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Morning's grace. ...It's still dark. I'll say it anyway. That's rather the point of me.
-> END

~ talk_devoted
if name:liriel_dawnsong and approval.liriel_dawnsong >= devoted and level >= 8
-> devoted
endif
-> END

~ devoted
Narrator: Liriel has been writing something in the back of her prayer book, very small. When she sees you looking, she turns the book round so you can read it. It's a list of your names.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: The novices write down whoever they pray for, so nobody is forgotten at the morning hymn. I started this in Death House. I've never had to cross anyone out. I mean to keep it that way.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: When I came here I thought I was carrying the dawn alone. My errand, and mine only, and you were kind people walking the same road.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I was wrong. It isn't something one person carries. It's heavier than that, and lighter. Do you understand? I'm not certain I do.
* We understand. -> devoted_understand
* Put yourself on the list, Liriel. -> devoted_list

~ devoted_understand
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Good. Then one of us does. That's enough for a congregation.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You understood what I meant about carrying the dawn
-> devoted_end

~ devoted_list
Narrator: She looks at the page a long moment. Then, at the very bottom, she writes her own name, in a hand much less steady than the others.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I've never done that. It feels terribly vain. ...It feels rather nice. Don't tell the Morninglord.
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You told me to put myself on my own prayer list
-> devoted_end

~ devoted_end
inspire name:liriel_dawnsong: knew the dawn isn't carried alone
-> END
